---
title: Tasks schema
description: The openschema/tasks contract — tasks with due dates, notes and subtasks.
---

`openschema/tasks` describes to-dos on the user's account. It's queryable structured data — see
[OpenSchema](/docs/neoworks/openschema) for the model and [contacts](/docs/neoworks/openschema/contacts) for a
related contract.

## Fields

```toml
[table.tasks]
columns = [
  { name = "title",     type = "string"   },
  { name = "due_at",    type = "datetime" },
  { name = "done",      type = "bool"     },
  { name = "note",      type = "string"   },
  { name = "contact",   type = "string"   },  # optional linked contact id
  { name = "parent",    type = "string"   },  # parent task id for subtasks
]
indexes = [
  { columns = ["user_id", "due_at"] }
]
```

`contact` references [`contacts`](/docs/neoworks/openschema/contacts); `parent` points at another task
row to form subtasks.

## Scopes

- `tasks:read` — read task titles, due dates, status.
- `tasks:write` — create, update and complete tasks.

## Querying

```sql
SELECT title, due_at FROM tasks
WHERE user_id = $auth.id AND done = false
ORDER BY due_at ASC;
```

